#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""talkstick: push-to-talk from an M5StickS3 (or anything speaking M5R1) to a command, a webhook or stdout.

Usage: talkstick [serve | bench WAV | fake-stick (WAV | --status | --ping) [HOST[:PORT]] | status | build-sink] [--dry]
Config: JSON at $TALKSTICK_CONFIG, else ~/.config/talkstick/config.json. See config.example.json.

Wire protocol M5R1 (one TCP connection per utterance, stick to daemon):
  stick sends  "M5R1 <device-id> <battery%> <fw-version>\\n", then frames of
               1 byte type + 2 bytes little-endian length + payload:
               A = audio (s16le PCM, 16 kHz, mono, up to 4096 bytes), E = end of utterance, C = cancel,
               S = status request (runs config status_prompt through delivery instead of audio),
               P = ping (daemon answers TIME and LAST, then closes).
  daemon sends UTF-8 lines: TIME <epoch> <utc-offset-s> (right after HELLO), RECV, WAIT <s>,
               SENT [first 40 chars], REPLY <text> (just before REPLIED), REPLIED, OFFLINE, ERR <reason>,
               LAST <text> (on ping, the last reply). REPLY and LAST text: at most stick_reply_chars (600)
               characters, newlines written as the two characters \\n.

Delivery contract
  print    The transcript is printed to the daemon's stdout. The stick sees SENT, then REPLIED.
  command  argv runs with the transcript on stdin (stdin is then closed). Env: TALKSTICK_DEVICE,
           TALKSTICK_UTTERANCE_ID, TALKSTICK_DRY ("1" in dry mode; the command must then not deliver).
           A stdout line "@sent" means the text was delivered: the stick sees SENT right away.
           Everything else on stdout is the reply. Exit 0 = REPLIED, exit 3 = target offline (OFFLINE),
           any other exit = ERR. No "@sent" before exit 0 means SENT is sent at exit.
  webhook  POST url with JSON {"text", "device", "utterance_id", "dry"}. A JSON body {"reply": "..."}
           or a plain-text body is the reply. 503 = offline. Other non-2xx = ERR.
  on_reply Optional argv run with the reply on stdin, trimmed to reply_max_chars plus reply_more_suffix.
           In dry mode it is printed, not run. offline_message, if set, goes through on_reply on OFFLINE.
"""
